{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 26, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0001-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0001", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "Students and the Form I-20", "text_sha256": "546163f433b4b59a0808aba4be0f7e9e96841aa948a2981a160110951d905911", "unit_text_sha256": "546163f433b4b59a0808aba4be0f7e9e96841aa948a2981a160110951d905911"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 309, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0002-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0002", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "All F and M students that study in the United States need a Form I-20, “Certificate of Eligibility for Nonimmigrant Student Status.” Once accepted into a Student and Exchange Visitor Program (SEVP)-certified school , nonimmigrant students will receive a Form I-20 from their designated school official (DSO) .", "text_sha256": "a7b44719abefce577ea1482b88028df0ac5b1ce7f851440bd5a3b5198a95e319", "unit_text_sha256": "a7b44719abefce577ea1482b88028df0ac5b1ce7f851440bd5a3b5198a95e319"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 528, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0003-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0003", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "You must also obtain a Form I-20 for any eligible dependents you plan to bring to the United States with you. However, please note that the name (i.e., Academic and Language students vs. Vocational Students) on the Form I-20 an SEVP-certified school issues you will dictate the type of student visa you may obtain from the U.S. Department of State and the status you will need to maintain in the United States. You and your DSO must both sign the Form I-20. If you are under age 18, your parents must sign the Form I-20 for you.", "text_sha256": "8f8214387c02e08b487973e093afbdaeb696a409be3dc1b59fdf80b47adf30f7", "unit_text_sha256": "8f8214387c02e08b487973e093afbdaeb696a409be3dc1b59fdf80b47adf30f7"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 128, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0004-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0004", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "The Form I-20 is an important document that you should keep safe, as you will need it throughout the F and M student life cycle.", "text_sha256": "821087ffc7ee9b2f41a9d30021e716afb598313b912be8ed3a630220d2397ae8", "unit_text_sha256": "821087ffc7ee9b2f41a9d30021e716afb598313b912be8ed3a630220d2397ae8"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 308, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0005-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0005", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "Before you pay the I-901 Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS) Fee, you must receive the Form I-20 from a DSO at the school you plan to attend. You will need information from the Form I-20 to pay the fee. The I-901 SEVIS Fee is mandatory and must be paid before you enter the United States.", "text_sha256": "334e37911e0d99801a8efa093f438c9c423fa19daa0d4af670f7a6009ec06d79", "unit_text_sha256": "334e37911e0d99801a8efa093f438c9c423fa19daa0d4af670f7a6009ec06d79"}
