{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 55, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0010-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0010", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "SEVIS Identification Number as listed on the Form I-20.", "text_sha256": "a9600bba2a167c18e06ccec16e7fa1b9aa996d9ba7e8bcdb604bb0ddf38fdd79", "unit_text_sha256": "a9600bba2a167c18e06ccec16e7fa1b9aa996d9ba7e8bcdb604bb0ddf38fdd79"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 526, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0011-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0011", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "The Form I-20 lists your program start date, 30 days before which you are allowed to enter the United States. F-1 and M-1 student visas can be issued up to 365 days in advance of your course of study start date. Your type of student visa must match the type of Form I-20 you have (e.g., F-1 or M-1). You are expected to have the original Form I-20 at your visa interview. The consular officer may accept a copy of the Form I-20 in limited circumstances that warrant visa issuance prior to you receiving the original Form I-20.", "text_sha256": "dd9be928ae002997038d8f265216d92e7a552076b208a754fbf84d70a3bc02d6", "unit_text_sha256": "dd9be928ae002997038d8f265216d92e7a552076b208a754fbf84d70a3bc02d6"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 309, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0012-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0012", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "You are expected to have the signed Form I-20 on hand as you enter the country. Do not pack it away in your suitcase. A U.S. Customs and Border Protection officer will instruct you to present your Form I-20 at the port of entry . You may arrive up to 30 days before the start date listed on your Form I-20; or", "text_sha256": "972c1e1a0ca624c29ce31d4847f605eb8c16c59d31e151f5f77aaf6a3156a9c3", "unit_text_sha256": "972c1e1a0ca624c29ce31d4847f605eb8c16c59d31e151f5f77aaf6a3156a9c3"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 155, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0013-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0013", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "You need a Form I-20 if you are already in the United States as another type of nonimmigrant and you are applying to USCIS to change your status to F or M.", "text_sha256": "caaa90296b222201a63b1e5c817f669b31c14ab31d0f6b795a3c88a24a4594cc", "unit_text_sha256": "caaa90296b222201a63b1e5c817f669b31c14ab31d0f6b795a3c88a24a4594cc"}
{"automatic_eligibility_rules_enabled": false, "category_candidate": "form_i20_guidance", "char_end": 311, "char_start": 0, "chunk_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0014-C001", "country": "US", "eligibility_rule_verified": false, "evidence_unit_id": "US-ST-01-S02-B0014", "heading": "Students and the Form I-20 | Study in the States", "physical_pdf_page": null, "printed_page_candidate": null, "program_id": "US-ST-01", "semantic_review_status": "needs_review", "side": null, "source_data_sha256": "4e2cbbb4b99d17a378e4bac1701bd57b1d1a340d536fd9e92c1d9899f2f26fa4", "source_kind": "official_html", "source_sha256": "becead6ca2f24032befa8dd000a6a060e873495b2c2c82239f42bd83c288893e", "source_url": "https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/students/prepare/students-and-the-form-i-20", "text": "Your Form I-20 proves that you are legally enrolled in a program of study in the United States. Therefore, it may be needed when you apply for the benefits available to F and M students. If you are eligible to apply for a driver’s license or a social security number , remember to bring your Form I-20 with you.", "text_sha256": "55b48f15182a85b319ba7dd747b74e30f49784388c5720e1233cfed7fef54b5f", "unit_text_sha256": "55b48f15182a85b319ba7dd747b74e30f49784388c5720e1233cfed7fef54b5f"}
